  '<p class="gd-p">Plans change. You can ask for more days, ask to change dates, answer a change we suggest, or cancel, all from your booking.</p><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-extend-your-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extend your rental</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Pick how long: <b class="gd-ui">1 hour</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 hours</b>, <b class="gd-ui">1 day</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 days</b>, <b class="gd-ui">1 week</b> or <b class="gd-ui">1 month</b>. Each shows the new return and its price, HST included: each added day costs your booking&#39;s price a day (what you paid for it, fees and HST included, divided by its days). An option the car cannot take is greyed out with the reason, and the page says until when the car is free.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> to pay with your card on file. When the car is free it is approved at once and the page shows your new return. No card on file, or the card is declined? The secure payment page opens: enter a card there. Otherwise the request goes to our team, and once approved you pay on the same page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For another date, open <b class="gd-ui">Another date and time</b>, choose it, press <b class="gd-ui">See the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Request extension</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/extend</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:960/552"><img src="/guides/img/renter-11-extend-desktop-957274cc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="960" height="552"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:34.4%;top:62.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.1%;top:77.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A few hours cost the hourly late fee, never more than a day, so extending never costs more than being late, and it keeps your trip covered. Already past your return time and still have the car? You can still extend. It counts from your original return time, and the late charges stay owed until the extension is paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-ask-to-change-dates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ask to change dates</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask to change dates</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Set the new pickup and return, then press <b class="gd-ui">See the difference</b> to see what you would pay or get back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask to change dates</b> to send it. Nothing changes until you agree to our answer.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/change</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:960/552"><img src="/guides/img/renter-12-change-desktop-09f6b563.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="960" height="552"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.1%;top:91.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-a-change-we-suggest" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A change we suggest</h2><p class="gd-p">Sometimes we need to change your booking, for example another car of the same class. You decide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an email, and your booking says &quot;We suggest a change to your booking&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review and answer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read what changes (before and after), the reason, the money and the time left to answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To agree, press <b class="gd-ui">Accept and sign the amendment</b>, sign, then press <b class="gd-ui">Accept and sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Anything more to pay is charged to your Card on File. If the card is declined, press <b class="gd-ui">Pay and apply the change</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">To say no, press <b class="gd-ui">Decline this change</b>. Your booking stays as it was.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>You have 48 hours to answer, and we send one reminder. CarmaCars signs the amendment at the moment you sign it, and the signed copy is saved under Documents. If the change costs less, the refund goes back to your card within 10 business days after the amendment is signed.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-cancel-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancel a booking</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read What you get back. It shows the rule that applies and your refund.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Type the booking number to confirm (for example CC-10021), then press <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/cancel</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/692"><img src="/guides/img/renter-13-cancel-desktop-d0bb2c67.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="692"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.1%;top:67.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.8%;top:45.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Standard booking: when you cancel</th><th scope="col">Refund of what you paid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, and 48 hours or more before pickup</td><td>95% back</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before pickup</td><td>75% back</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before pickup</td><td>50% back</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 24 hours before pickup</td><td>No refund</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">A Non-refundable booking gets no refund. The deposit is taken at pickup, so none is held when you cancel before it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-messages-tolls-and-tickets" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Messages, tolls and tickets</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>On a rental of 2 days or more we check in after the first day: &quot;How is the car?&quot; If anything is off, reply to the email or text, or call us.</li><li>Write to us about a booking at the bottom of its page: type in Your message and press Send.</li><li>Tolls and tickets are yours to pay, including Highway 407 ETR. If one reaches us, we pay it and charge the amount plus our fee to your Card on File, and email you a copy of the notice.</li><li>Running late? Extend in your booking, even after the return time while you still have the car, or call us at 289-312-5991. The late fee is 17.5% of the daily rate for each started hour (at least $25) after a 30 minute grace.</li><li>Before your return we remind you: the day before, about 3 hours before (with an Extend link) and at the return time. If the car is late we send a notice at 15 minutes and a final notice at 2 hours. No late notices between 10 pm and 7 am.</li><li>Already brought the car back but still getting late notices? Tap <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> in the notice, or press it on your booking. Add photos of the car where you left it (pick several at once from your camera roll), the odometer, the fuel level and the time you returned it: all optional. The late notices stop at once while we check. When we confirm, your trip is complete. If we cannot find the car, we tell you why and the notices start again.</li><li>Something wrong with the car? While you have it, press <b class="gd-ui">Report a problem</b> on your booking: it calls roadside help, or opens a message to us.</li><li>Someone else will drive too? Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a driver</b>: write their name in the message and we add them; they sign with their own link.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-return-the-car-yourself-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Return the car yourself (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Return the car yourself</b> on your booking: photos of the car where you left it, the odometer, the fuel and the time. With all of them your trip is completed at once and any late notices stop; we may still adjust the readings after we see the car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-report-an-accident" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Report an accident</h2><p class="gd-p">While you have the car, the <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b> on your booking has <b class="gd-ui">Report an accident</b>. Anyone hurt? Call 911 first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Say what happened, when (empty means now) and where: type it or press <b class="gd-ui">Use my location</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add photos and videos from your camera roll: all the cars, the plates, the damage and the scene.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add the other party&#39;s name, phone, plate and their insurer, and the police report number if there is one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Answer <b class="gd-ui">Is anyone hurt?</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Can the car be driven?</b>, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the report</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Your answers stay on your phone as you type until you send them. Once sent, our team has it at once and calls you; the page shows the next steps, <b class="gd-ui">Call us</b>, and lets you add more photos or videos.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-extend-at-the-same-rate-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extend at the same rate (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An extension costs the same a day as your booking, and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan are charged for the added days at the same rate. Delivery is never charged again. The price shows before you ask.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-secondary-contact-and-rideshare-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Secondary contact and rideshare documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">More</b> on your booking page:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Secondary contact</b>: someone we may call if we cannot reach you, for this trip or on your profile. Optional.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Rideshare or delivery documents</b>: rideshare and delivery driving are welcome. Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform? Pick the platforms and print the documents they ask for: your rental agreement, a coverage letter and a vehicle letter.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-rideshare-a-second-contact-and-a-mid-trip-check-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rideshare, a second contact and a mid-trip check (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform is allowed: your booking page makes the documents they ask for.</li><li>Add a secondary contact we can call if we cannot reach you, on your profile or for one trip.</li><li>Halfway through a longer trip we send one short message asking how it is going. Reply with any problem and our team picks it up.</li><li>We send no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning. Common questions are answered at once, and a person answers anything else.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-deposit-still-owed-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit still owed (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">If you picked up the car before the deposit hold was placed, your booking page says <b class="gd-ui">Deposit still owed</b> with the amount. It is a hold on your credit card, not a charge, released after the rental. We try your saved card each morning; if that does not work we send you a secure link by text or email. Tap it to place the hold, or call us.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-notices-from-the-car-s-tracker-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Notices from the car&#39;s Tracker (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car has a Tracker, as your rental agreement says (section 12). If it records something, we tell you at once by email, text or the app: what happened, any charge, and the clause of your agreement.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h</b>: one speeding charge an event, at the highest limit reached ($500, $1,000 or $2,500 plus HST). It is taken from your deposit first.</li><li>A speed well over the limit, or hard braking: a friendly heads-up. No charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The car outside Ontario, past its return time, or its Tracker unplugged</b>: please call us.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The car at an impound lot</b>: call us at once so we can get it released. The towing and storage costs are yours.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the notice, or your booking page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call us if something is wrong or you have a question. We would rather sort it out with you.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>You can turn the heads-up messages off under <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>. Notices about a charge are always sent.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'home-and-your-vehicles', 'chapter', 'apply-and-get-your-car-listed', 'Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.

## Home at a glance

1. The menu: Home, Cars (your cars and their bookings), Money (statements, payouts and invoices), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications). Each of Cars, Money and Account is one page with a row of tabs on top. Home starts with the next thing to do, then one line with what you earned so far this month, how many cars are out, the next payout and any fees due.
2. At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month''s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.
3. Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or **Payouts** for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.
4. Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press **Add a vehicle**.

![](/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1270; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 19.1 8.1, 2 72.9 30.7, 3 31.2 85.0")

> Tip: When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.

## A car''s page

Open Cars, then a car.

1. The top shows the car''s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.
2. Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.
3. This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. **Book it for myself** reserves it for you.
4. Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.

![](/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1242; address: carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7; pins: 1 55.6 25.1, 2 83.3 38.0, 3 36.5 54.5, 4 81.2 67.0")

While a car is being set up, its page also shows the **Onboarding** checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender''s permission and the insurance.

## Where your car is

Once your car has its tracker, its page shows **Where your car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported, and **Open on the map**. Below it, the trips of the last 30 days: when, how far, and where each started and ended.

1. Open **Cars** and the car.
2. No tracker on the car yet? It says **No tracker yet**.
3. You see the location and the trips only. The renter''s name and the booking stay private, as before.

## The onboarding checklist

Home and each car''s page show the same **Onboarding checklist**. Each step says one of four things: done, to do (and who it waits on: you, CarmaCars, or another office such as the registry), blocked (and why, for example "First: terms approved"), or not needed. A step that waits on you has one button: the one thing to do for it, such as **Check and sign** or **Upload the ownership permit**.

## Change an onboarding photo

A wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter? Open the car, then **Your onboarding photos**.

1. Press **Replace** and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.
2. Or press **Remove**, then **Remove the photo**.

> Good to know: Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.

## Add several cars at once

Open **Cars**, then **Add cars from a VIN list**.

1. Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.
2. Press **Preview**: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.
3. Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press **Add**.

Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.

## Service and maintenance

On a car''s page, under Service and maintenance.

- What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.
- Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.
- You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.
- It is read only: call or message us about a service.

## Take new listing photos

Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.

1. On the car''s page, press **Add listing photos** (or **Take new photos** for a car already live).
2. Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot in the list. Press **Retake** if one is not right.
4. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
5. Press **Submit for listing**. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg "phone; size: 390 610; pins: 4 92.3 43.4, 3 76.9 70.2")

## Price limits

Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.

1. **Cars**, **Price limits for every car**, at the bottom: type a **Minimum a day** and a **Maximum a day** in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press **Save price limits**.
2. One car different? Open it: **Price limits** has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.
3. Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.

## Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** shows the car''s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, **Cars** > **Cars you referred** shows their cars'' bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.

## Studio photos (release 48)

- We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.
- Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.
- We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in **Account**, **Notifications**.
