- What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.
- Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.
- You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.
- It is read only: call or message us about a service.

## Take new listing photos

Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.

1. On the car''s page, press **Add listing photos** (or **Take new photos** for a car already live).
2. Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot in the list. Press **Retake** if one is not right.
4. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
5. Press **Submit for listing**. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg "phone; size: 390 610; pins: 4 92.3 43.4, 3 76.9 70.2")

## Price limits

Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.

1. **Cars**, **Price limits for every car**, at the bottom: type a **Minimum a day** and a **Maximum a day** in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press **Save price limits**.
2. One car different? Open it: **Price limits** has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.
3. Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.

## Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** shows the car''s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, **Cars** > **Cars you referred** shows their cars'' bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.

## Studio photos (release 48)

- We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.
- Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.
- We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in **Account**, **Notifications**.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.</p><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-home-at-a-glance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Home at a glance</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The menu: Home, Cars (your cars and their bookings), Money (statements, payouts and invoices), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications). Each of Cars, Money and Account is one page with a row of tabs on top. Home starts with the next thing to do, then one line with what you earned so far this month, how many cars are out, the next payout and any fees due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month&#39;s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or <b class="gd-ui">Payouts</b> for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a vehicle</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1270"><img src="/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1270"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.1%;top:8.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:30.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.2%;top:85%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-a-car-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Cars, then a car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The top shows the car&#39;s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. <b class="gd-ui">Book it for myself</b> reserves it for you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1242"><img src="/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1242"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:55.6%;top:25.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:38%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.5%;top:54.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:67%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">While a car is being set up, its page also shows the <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender&#39;s permission and the insurance.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-where-your-car-is" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where your car is</h2><p class="gd-p">Once your car has its tracker, its page shows <b class="gd-ui">Where your car is</b>: moving or parked, when it last reported, and <b class="gd-ui">Open on the map</b>. Below it, the trips of the last 30 days: when, how far, and where each started and ended.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> and the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">No tracker on the car yet? It says <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You see the location and the trips only. The renter&#39;s name and the booking stay private, as before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-tracker-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Once your car has its tracker, its page shows <b class="gd-ui">Tracker alerts</b> below <b class="gd-ui">Where your car is</b>: what the tracker recorded in the last 30 days.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Speeding, harsh driving, the car outside Ontario, driving after the return time, the tracker unplugged or tampered with, or the car parked at an impound lot.</li><li>Each alert says what happened and when, with <b class="gd-ui">See the place</b>.</li><li>We also tell you by email, text or the app when one happens.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> and the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing there? It says nothing was recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To stop these alerts or change how they reach you, open <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b> and turn <b class="gd-ui">Tracker alert on your car</b> off or on.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>There is nothing for you to do. CarmaCars handles each one with the renter and collects any charge with its evidence. You see the event and the place only, never the renter or the booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-the-onboarding-checklist" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The onboarding checklist</h2><p class="gd-p">Home and each car&#39;s page show the same <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>. Each step says one of four things: done, to do (and who it waits on: you, CarmaCars, or another office such as the registry), blocked (and why, for example &quot;First: terms approved&quot;), or not needed. A step that waits on you has one button: the one thing to do for it, such as <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Upload the ownership permit</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-change-an-onboarding-photo" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an onboarding photo</h2><p class="gd-p">A wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter? Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Your onboarding photos</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove the photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-add-several-cars-at-once" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add several cars at once</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a VIN list</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-service-and-maintenance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Service and maintenance</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, under Service and maintenance.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.</li><li>Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.</li><li>You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.</li><li>It is read only: call or message us about a service.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-take-new-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take new listing photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the car&#39;s page, press <b class="gd-ui">Add listing photos</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Take new photos</b> for a car already live).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot in the list. Press <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if one is not right.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/610"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="610"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.3%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:70.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-price-limits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Price limits</h2><p class="gd-p">Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Price limits for every car</b>, at the bottom: type a <b class="gd-ui">Minimum a day</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Maximum a day</b> in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One car different? Open it: <b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b> has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-pickup-and-return-records-cars-you-referred-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> shows the car&#39;s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> shows their cars&#39; bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-studio-photos-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio photos (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.</li><li>Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio phot